Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Preserve deferred CONTAINING regions and mappings

Parameterized CHOICE types can carry size determinants for alternatives that
use CONTAINING. Deferred ACN generation discarded the containing-region
boundary when it crossed the CHOICE reference and emitted a patched length
without its ACN mapping function. The generated program then encoded and
decoded against the outer stream rather than the selected alternative's
bounded region, and mapped determinants used the unmapped length.

Carry the containing-region and mapping information through deferred
specialization, and extend the language template interface consistently. C
and Ada apply the mapping function, Rust follows its existing mapping
convention, and the currently stubbed Python and Scala deferred backends accept
the same interface.

Add nested and mapped CONTAINING regressions. Besides generated round trips,
the mapped case asserts the exact encoded bytes and verifies decoding, so the
test proves that the mapping is applied rather than merely compiling the
generated source.

